      },
      "reason": "CN-01 asks for two things: a batch declares no line figure, and a batch's per-scope total is derived from its member task estimates instead, so no second declaration can drift away from the first. The part concerning BatchDeclaration is the absence, and that absence is guaranteed by the type rather than by behaviour. The declaration holds an identifier and an ordered list of member task ids; its whole declared surface — new(id, task_ids), id(), task_ids(), contains(task_id) — takes no line quantity in, stores none, and returns none. There is therefore no state in which a declared batch total could exist to disagree with the members it summarises, and no run-time observation that could distinguish a compliant declaration from a non-compliant one: a non-compliant one is not constructible. The remaining half of the constraint, the derivation of the per-scope total as the sum of the member estimates, is not this entry's either — BatchDeclaration is handed no estimate at all, and the derivation is declared on the aggregate that holds the estimates. Nothing in this declaration is left over that a test could exercise for CN-01."
    },
