      "reason": "AC-01 is checked by two observations: that batch-plan.json exists as a Phase 3 planning artifact, and that its writer is restricted to impl-planner — recorded in the peer capability contracts' writes-forbidden lists, with the admission-deciding CLI reading only. BatchPlanDocument is the in-memory model of that artifact's content and touches no file system, so it cannot observe whether the file exists, and it holds no notion of an author, a capability contract or a writes-forbidden list. The one part that might look testable — that consumers only read — is a property of the declaration rather than of behaviour: the type offers a constructor and borrowing accessors (track_id, task_estimates, batches, estimate_for, batch_of, scope_total, current_batch) and no mutator at all, so a consumer that edits a plan through this type is not expressible and no test can distinguish a read-only consumer from a writing one. Whatever a test asserted here would restate the type system or the absence of file access rather than AC-01's promise; the evidence the anchor asks for lives in the capability contracts and in the CLI wiring."
